<title>USA: Time Warner plans layoffs, cost cuts - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Time Warner plans layoffs, cost cuts - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc, fresh from getting regulatory approval of its $6.5 billion acquisition of Turner Broadcasting System Inc, plans layoffs, asset sales and other cost-cutting measures, the Wall Street Journal reported Friday.</p>
<p>In a memo to employees at both companies, a committee of Time Warner and Turner executives said Time Warner will try achieve $200 million to $300 million in cost savings after the merger is complete, the article said.</p>
<p>The brunt of the initiatives were expected to be felt at Turner Broadcasting, where Chairman Ted Turner recently told employees that the merger would cut as many as 1,000 jobs and $100 million in expenses, according to the article.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
</text>
